Implement a sign extension circuit that takes a 16-bit signed input and extends it to a 32-bit signed output. The most significant bit (MSB) of the 16-bit input determines the value of the upper 16 bits of the output, ensuring that the output maintains the correct sign. If the MSB is 1 (indicating a negative value), the upper 16 bits of the output are filled with 1s; if the MSB is 0, they are filled with 0s. The lower 16 bits of the output match the input directly.
