description:
Design a digital potentiometer that uses control signals to adjust the resistance based on a given input. The module accepts a control input vector of width 'n' and an 8-bit data input, which collectively determine the output resistance value. The calculated resistance is then scaled relative to a fixed total resistance of the potentiometer. The output is a 'n'-bit wide value representing the adjusted resistance, enabling programmable control of resistance in electronic circuits.
