description:
Design a PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) generator that takes a clock signal and a 4-bit duty cycle input to control the width of the output pulse. The module increments a counter on each clock cycle and resets it after reaching a maximum value of 15. The output `pwm_out` will be high for a duration proportional to the `duty_cycle`, allowing for adjustable brightness or signal modulation based on the duty cycle value.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input [3:0] duty_cycle,
    output reg pwm_out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input [3:0] duty_cycle,
    output reg pwm_out
);reg [3:0] counter;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    counter <= counter + 1;
    if (counter >= 15) begin
        counter <= 0;
        pwm_out <= (counter < duty_cycle);
    end
end

endmodule

